# interplay_lifetime_held_pipeline_function_retyped: A compute pipeline (double_gid) dispatched, then dispatched again by an exec held on the gate while the worker deletes objects with DeleteObject (40): the pipeline (operation 1006), which the released exec makes again from its record and runs; its function (1005) with the pipeline live, which changes nothing; the pipeline with its entry then retyped 0, so the release faults ("Failed to create ComputePipelineState"); and both, with the function's entry retyped 0: making the pipeline again looks its function up from the empty entry, which raises the function lookup's failure, so the release faults ("function lookup failed") in every setup, where a nil function would have Metal abort (docs/testing.md, section 7.4).
